From f4d6389de2ee041528ba296d3b4cd08ca2014470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:21:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci-domain: baldur: use the system domain state
 only in system suspend

On the Lenovo TB323FU (SM8850) the tablet reset silently now and then
while it sat idle with the display off or was turning the display on:
no oops, panic or lockup in the printk ring, straight to the firmware
dump mode. Reading the crashed kernel out of the full DDR dump with drgn
showed every CPU idle, CPUs 0-4 of cluster0 having entered retention
(cpu-sleep-0) within 20 ms and never leaving it again -- IPIs queued in
call_single_queue/ttwu_pending, hrtimers long expired -- while CPUs 5-7
kept running for about ten seconds until the SoC was reset.

A display on/off and s2idle loop hit it about once in 25 cycles.
Disabling the CPU retention state, dropping both domain states, or
dropping only the system domain state (domain-sleep-0) each ran 60
cycles clean (0 in 180), with the cluster state and CPU retention still
in use hundreds of thousands of times. Dropping the system domain state
costs CX/DDR collapse in s2idle though (about 89 mA instead of 18-35 mA).

Keep the system domain state for system-wide suspend, like PREEMPT_RT
does for all CPU domains, with GENPD_FLAG_RPM_ALWAYS_ON on that domain:
60 cycles clean, and CX collapses for the whole of a 4.8 h s2idle.

Board-local workaround; the root cause is in firmware or the wake path
and is not understood.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
index b9e4ad7d4..08e166ccc 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/cpu.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_domain.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
@@ -71,6 +72,10 @@ static int psci_pd_init(struct device_node *np, bool use_osi)
 		pd->flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP;
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT))
 			pd->flags |= GENPD_FLAG_RPM_ALWAYS_ON;
+		/* from runtime idle it can leave CPUs in retention for good */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") &&
+		    of_node_name_eq(np, "power-domain-system"))
+			pd->flags |= GENPD_FLAG_RPM_ALWAYS_ON;
 	} else {
 		pd->flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
 	}
-- 
